title: Genesis 10 – The Nations of Men
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 10: the seventy nations descended from the three sons of Noah, and the God who sets the bounds of their habitation.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-10-table-of-nations.html

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own sentences from the Genesis 10 study (post 6674).

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 10 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 10: The Nations of Men
sub: Japheth • Ham • Shem • Seventy Nations
refs: Genesis 10:1-32
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The sons of Japheth
--- The Generations of the Sons of Noah
kicker: v. 1
sub: Unto Them Were Sons Born After the Flood
scripture: Genesis 10:1
p: And so we have the division of man into races and nations. 70 different ethnic tribes, descended from the three sons of Noah. God commanded them to be fruitful and replenish the earth. [[Genesis 9:1]]

--- The Sons of Japheth
kicker: vv. 2–5
sub: The Isles of the Gentiles Divided
scripture: Genesis 10:2-5 | mark: every one after his tongue, after their families, in their nations
p: Much has been made of this account, and conclusions drawn from the curse of Canaan through Ham, the Ashkenaz being of Japheth, not Shem, and so on.

=== The sons of Ham
--- The Sons of Ham
kicker: vv. 6–7
sub: Cush, Mizraim, Phut, and Canaan
scripture: Genesis 10:6-7

--- Nimrod
kicker: vv. 8–12
sub: A Mighty Hunter Before the {Lord}
scripture: Genesis 10:8-12 | mark: the beginning of his kingdom was Babel
p: Nimrod founded Babel and the great cities of the land of Shinar. We look at what is said of him, and what isn’t, in [[lesson:genesis-11-tower-of-babel|Genesis 11]].

--- Mizraim and Canaan
kicker: vv. 13–18
sub: The Families of the Canaanites Spread Abroad
scripture: Genesis 10:13-18

--- The Border of the Canaanites
kicker: vv. 19–20
sub: The Land Promised to Abram’s Seed
scripture: Genesis 10:19-20 | mark: the border of the Canaanites
p: The sons of Canaan, whose land would be given to Abram’s seed. [[Genesis 9:25]] [[Genesis 15:18-21]]

=== The sons of Shem
--- The Sons of Shem
kicker: vv. 21–25
sub: For in His Days Was the Earth Divided
scripture: Genesis 10:21-25 | mark: for in his days was the earth divided

--- The Sons of Joktan
kicker: vv. 26–30
sub: From Mesha unto Sephar
scripture: Genesis 10:26-30

--- By These Were the Nations Divided
kicker: vv. 31–32
sub: After Their Generations, in Their Nations
scripture: Genesis 10:31-32 | mark: by these were the nations divided in the earth after the flood

=== What the lists tell us
--- When the Bible Gets into Lists of Names
kicker: Application
sub: What the Genealogies Tell Us
p: I won’t lie, when the Bible gets into lists of names, I glaze over. Genealogies tell me that scripture is a historical account of man. That God sets the nations and their borders and habitations thereof. That God judges nations of men on earth, blessing them, cursing them, and at times erasing them.

--- God Sets the Bounds
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 10:32
fig: Acts 17:26 | Acts 17:26 | God sets the nations and their borders, and the habitations thereof.
fig: Genesis 11:8-9 | Genesis 11:8-9 | When the nations unite under a one world government of men, they challenge God. And so God scatters them.

--- The Nations of Men
center: The speculation of men like Josephus and later historians, tracing the migration and evolution of the 70 original nations to today, is very popular, and for many, these lists and maps fascinate. Have at it. But the lists tell us this: scripture is history, and God sets the bounds of the nations and judges them.
